From f8989e8d73135f4d3f386caa1f17e5f17777ed70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:44:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): upstream-sync diagnostics review fixes: exact-set
 owner only, first-parent base, bounded nightly reads [daveey]

- A nightly card owning main's (different) failing set is labelled as main's set's owner, never
  as the owner of the candidate's exact set.
- The baseline is the sync's first parent when it is on main (merge-base only as fallback): after
  criss-cross syncs merge-base could return an upstream commit.
- baseline runs are read once per refusal; nightlies are filtered server-side to completed
  dispatches created after the base commit, newest 10 checked.
- A skipped/cancelled required job is labelled with its conclusion, not as "failed".
- OPEN comes from flaky_kanban. Tests: ci.yaml e2e baseline, partial slice set, both kinds,
  fork-point fallback, main-set owner labelling.
---
